# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
# Every environment variable the project uses must be listed here with a safe
# placeholder, added in the same change that introduces it.
#
# **Every variable below is read by the code.** That was not true until D-055: eleven were
# listed here and read by nothing, which is worse than omitting them — a variable that looks
# like configuration and silently does nothing costs an afternoon to discover.

# --- Application ---
# APP_ENV was listed here and read by nothing; it is gone.
LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Backend server ---
# The application binds to loopback. It is single-user and unauthenticated;
# exposing it on a network interface would publish an unauthenticated
# transcript of a private room.
API_HOST=127.0.0.1
API_PORT=8395

# --- Configuration ---
# Where the user configuration file is read and written. Defaults to
# ./data/loud-radish-config.json when unset. Credentials are NEVER written here.
# LOUD_RADISH_CONFIG_PATH=./data/loud-radish-config.json
#
# Renamed in D-038. The pre-rename names are still read so an existing install keeps
# working, and using one logs a warning: TRANSCRIBER_CONFIG_PATH, TRANSCRIBER_ROOT,
# TRANSCRIBER_NO_GPU_REPAIR. Do not set them in new installs.
#
# Where the repository lives, for the tray companion's shortcut commands. Defaults to
# the working directory.
# LOUD_RADISH_ROOT=.
#
# Set to 1 to stop the launcher reinstalling the kept ROCm wheel.
# LOUD_RADISH_NO_GPU_REPAIR=1

# --- Storage ---
DATA_DIR=./data
# LOG_DIR and SESSION_DIR were listed here and were also read by nothing. The session directory is
# `storage.session_dir` in the configuration, not an environment variable.

# --- Speech recognition and the language model ---
# There are no environment variables for these, and there never were. This file used to list
# ASR_BACKEND, ASR_MODEL, ASR_DEVICE, LLM_MODE, LLM_LOCAL_ENDPOINT, LLM_LOCAL_MODEL,
# LLM_API_PROVIDER and LLM_API_MODEL — and no Python read a single one of them, so setting any of
# them did nothing at all while looking exactly like configuration (D-055).
#
# Configuration flows through ConfigStore's four layers only: built-in defaults, the user file at
# LOUD_RADISH_CONFIG_PATH, per-session overrides, and what the settings interface writes at
# runtime. Change the model in Settings -> Transcription, or edit the user file.

# --- Credentials ---
# API keys are read from the OS credential store (`keyring`, a core dependency since D-023).
# These environment variables are the fallback.
# Never commit a real value; never log one; never send one to the frontend.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
